sentences.text:
The prayers in the leading writ petition are as follows.-
I. Issue an appropriate writ, order or direction quashing the circle rate determined by the District Collector, District Mathura in the year 2016 and 2017;
II. Issue an appropriate writ, order or direction commanding the District Collector, District Mathura to revise the circle rate of the petitioner's land situated in Village Alhepur, Post Chattikara, Tehsil and Pargana Mathura, District Mathura;
III. Issue an appropriate writ, order or direction commanding the Divisional Commissioner to forthwith take necessary action upon the complaint made by the petitioner on 02.02.2020;
IV. Issue an appropriate writ, order or direction quashing the decision taken by the Committee on 26.05.2018 constituted by the respondent No. 4.
V. Issue an appropriate writ, order or direction commanding the Additional District Magistrate (Land Acquisition/Special Land Acquisition Officer to determine the market value of the land on the basis of the circle rates being revised by the District Collector and declare the award in accordance with the provisions of the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition,
Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013;
VI. Issue an appropriate writ, order or direction commanding the respondents to provide alternative land to the land owners for their personal occupation.
